available lengths: 150cm, 154cm, 156cm, 158cm, 162cm, 154cm Wide, 158cm Wide, 162cm Wide, 166cm Wide
board type: All Mountain
rider level: Intermediate / Expert
flex: 4.5/10
flex pattern: Twin Flex (flexes the same in nose and tail)
shape: Directional (slightly longer nose than tail for pop in tail and extra float)
camber type: Flying V (blend of playful rocker with camber underfoot for versatility)
mounting system: The Channel (Burton Channel system, compatible with most major binding brands, works best with Burton EST bindings)
core: Super Fly II 700G (stronger and lighter woods targeted in specific areas for pop and strength while reducing weight)
core zones: Dualzone EGD (wood grain along heel and toe edge in two unbroken zones perpendicular to rest of core for consistent edge hold and strength)
core sections: Squeezebox (thicker more powerful sections combined with thinner more flexible sections profiled throughout core for enhanced energy transfer)
carbon: 45° Carbon Highlights (tip to tail carbon layer reduces weight, 45° angled fibres fine tune torsional flex)
base: Sintered WFO (Wide F!#@ing Open - extra absorbent high density sintered material infused with specially formulated wax)
durability technology: Infinite Ride (boards overbuilt in factory then broken down by machinery to ride consistently from day one to day 100)
tip/tail technology: Pro Tip (tip and tail taper out at points reducing swing weight and promoting mobility)
edges: Frostbite Edges (edges extend out slightly underneath bindings for enhanced edge hold on hardpack and ice)
resin: Super Sap Epoxy (bio-based resin reducing carbon footprint by 50% over conventional petroleum-based epoxies)
shipping restriction: Only available for shipping within Australia
alternative version: Custom also available in Camber bend
